<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PROPOSAL 56 Q5.1 (QBX-271, nassau-digital GATES Q5, DESIGN §9.4).
  NASSAUDIGITAL IS PLAYED LIVE THROUGH THE LIVE LANE, TRANSPORT STOPPED.

  The same path and the same measurement as live_instrument_play, with the
  sampler in slot 0 instead of the test sine: CaptureMidiInput (midi-in-event)
  -> MidiInFanout -> the consumer ring -> twLiveEventSource::collect ON THE
  PUMP inside twPluginSlotProcessor::render -> twSamplerInstrument::process
  -> the live ring -> the RT callback. Nothing in the live lane names the
  sampler (proposal 56 §4.9); this case is the evidence that nothing has to.
  sampler_q5_live_playing is the same claim with the transport running, and
  the one in which the ownership assertion has teeth.

  THE FIXTURE. One zone over every key, root 60, one-shot, one file layer:
  ../test_stereo.wav, 3 s of a 480 Hz sine, ch0 rms 0.49999, ch1 rms 0.24999.
  Velocity 127 plays the layer at unity, so a second after the onset the
  capture reads the sample's own levels (Q0 measured 0.49997 / 0.24998 through
  the offline render; here 0.499971 / 0.249976 through the live lane).

  THE ONSET BOUND, 7168 frames = 7 blocks at the headless 1024-frame device
  block. It is the live lane's own worst case, the one live_instrument_play
  derives: the ring is twLiveMixRingDefaultDepth = 4 blocks deep, the pump
  covers lead = 2 blocks ahead of the frame the RT pulls next (playback inv.
  16), and that frame is one device block past the one being delivered:
  4 + 2 + 1 = 7 blocks (proposal 21 L2 AC1). live_instrument_play asserts
  12288 for headroom; this case asserts the derived number, because the
  sabotage that holds the sampler's notes back three blocks lands at 8003
  frames and would pass 12288. assert-audio-onset prints the measured lag on
  every run.

  THE REFERENCE, FROM THE SAME NOTE. Track 1 holds the test sine, armed on
  the same MIDI input. The sampler is panned hard left and the sine hard
  right, so the capture's channel 0 is the sampler alone and channel 1 the
  sine alone, and one injected note plays both in the same pump blocks. The
  difference of their onsets (refChannel) carries none of the scheduling
  jitter each absolute lag does, so it can be bounded tightly: 64 frames, the
  onset scan's window. A sampler one device block late (1024) passes the
  absolute bound and fails this one. It is GATES Q5.2's comparison, made
  headless with an instrument whose own cost is nil in place of
  nassau-analogue.

  MEASURED (QBX-271, the dev box, 12 cores, load average 5 to 15, other
  agents' gates running): the sampler's onset lag 4646 to 4936 frames
  (96.8 to 102.8 ms) over 25 runs, the sine's exactly one frame later in
  every run (difference -1: the sampler's sinc reader crosses the threshold a
  frame before the sine's first cycle does). Levels 0.499971 (the sample's
  left channel at unity) and 0.707205 (the sine at velocity 127, amplitude
  1). The single-track form of this case measured 4002 to 5039 at load
  average 11 to 40. The latency is the lane's, not the sampler's.

  afterMidiIn="1" maps the injection's host time to a capture frame through
  CaptureBackend::frameAtHostTime, the audio backend's own block log, which
  shares no code with the pump, the ring or the event source.

  RUN_SERIAL at SMARAGD_CAPTURE_SPEED=1 (smaragd/CMakeLists.txt), like the
  live_instrument_* cases: the onset is a wall-clock latency, so it measures
  the box as well as the code. Read /proc/loadavg before reading a failure as
  a regression.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="sampler_q5_live_play">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0"
                   format="tw" uid="tw.native.nassaudigital"
                   name="NassauDigital" vendor="Nassau"
                   path="" nIn="0" nOut="2"/>
    <assert-instrument-slot trackPath="0" present="1" format="tw"
                            uid="tw.native.nassaudigital" mode="DirectGen"
                            state="Active" hasFeed="1"/>
    <add-zone trackPath="0" slotIndex="0" keyLo="0" keyHi="127" rootKey="60" mode="oneshot">
      <layer src="file:../test_stereo.wav"/>
    </add-zone>
    <wait-sampler-generations trackPath="0" slotIndex="0" timeoutMs="15000"/>
    <assert-sampler-layer trackPath="0" slotIndex="0" layer="2" generation="1"
                          rendering="0" installs="1"/>

    <!-- THE REFERENCE: the test sine every live_instrument_* case plays, on
         track 1. The sampler is panned hard LEFT and the sine hard RIGHT, so
         ONE note gives each instrument a channel of its own. -->
    <insert-plugin trackPath="1" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.sine"
                   name="Smaragd Test Sine" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="0" nOut="2"
                   isInstrument="true"/>
    <set-track-pan trackPath="0" pan="-1"/>
    <set-track-pan trackPath="1" pan="1"/>

    <!-- The live input, and the ARM with the transport stopped: Monitor Auto
         is the tape machine, so stopped means the input is live. -->
    <set-track-input trackPath="0" input="midi:capture:any"/>
    <set-track-input trackPath="1" input="midi:capture:any"/>
    <arm-track trackPath="0" armed="1"/>
    <arm-track trackPath="1" armed="1"/>
    <assert-input-meter trackPath="0" contains="live=on"/>
    <wait-ms ms="600"/>

    <midi-in-event kind="noteon" key="60" velocity="127" channel="0"/>
    <wait-ms ms="1500"/>
    <dump-playback-capture filename="sq5_live.wav" minFrames="72000"/>

    <!-- Q5.1: HOW LATE, in frames, against the audio block log: the
         sampler (channel 0), then the reference (channel 1), same bound. -->
    <assert-audio-onset filename="sq5_live.wav" afterMidiIn="1" channel="0"
                        threshold="0.05" maxFrame="7168"/>
    <assert-audio-onset filename="sq5_live.wav" afterMidiIn="1" channel="1"
                        threshold="0.05" maxFrame="7168"/>
    <!-- ...and the sampler against the reference, from the SAME note: what
         the sampler adds over an instrument with no cost at all. 64 frames is
         the onset scan's own window; one device block late would be 1024. -->
    <assert-audio-onset filename="sq5_live.wav" channel="0" refChannel="1"
                        threshold="0.05" maxFrame="64"/>
    <!-- ...and each channel holds its own instrument alone, half a second
         after the onset: the sample's left channel at unity (0.49999), and
         the sine at velocity 127, amplitude 1 (rms 0.70711). -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="sq5_live.wav" channel="0" anchorOnset="1"
                         startFrame="24000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.48" maxRms="0.52"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="sq5_live.wav" channel="1" anchorOnset="1"
                         startFrame="24000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.69" maxRms="0.72"/>

    <arm-track trackPath="0" armed="0"/>
    <arm-track trackPath="1" armed="0"/>
    <!-- Q5.1: no ownership refusal. With the transport stopped nothing
         demands a freeze of the track, so this is a necessary condition
         here and a real one in sampler_q5_live_playing. -->
    <assert-render-policy liveThreadRefusals="0" liveOwnedRefusals="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="2"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
